From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:46:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: no EGL device query in the GPU module

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: the EGL headers of AROS nightly 2026-11-24 declare the device
extensions, which turns on the EGL device query of the GPU module. It
calls eglGetProcAddress, which egl.library does not export, so the
program did not link against that SDK.
Solution: leave the EGL device query out on AROS. The cards are read
from pci.hidd (gpu_aros.c).
Scope: detection/gpu/gpu.c, one preprocessor condition; AROS only.
Upstream-Status: AROS-specific.
Verification: links with the SDK of nightly 2026-11-24; the GPU module
is the pci.hidd one as before.
Removal: when egl.library exports eglGetProcAddress.
---
 src/detection/gpu/gpu.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/detection/gpu/gpu.c b/src/detection/gpu/gpu.c
index b1e266d..b081261 100644
--- a/src/detection/gpu/gpu.c
+++ b/src/detection/gpu/gpu.c
@@ -149,7 +149,8 @@ const char* detectByOpenGL(FFlist* gpus) {
     return error;
 }
 
-#if defined(FF_HAVE_EGL) || __has_include(<EGL/egl.h>)
+/* AROS: egl.library has no eglGetProcAddress; cards come from pci.hidd. */
+#if (defined(FF_HAVE_EGL) || __has_include(<EGL/egl.h>)) && !defined(__AROS__)
     #include <EGL/egl.h>
     #include <EGL/eglext.h>
 
